{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Gender Issues", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Battle of the Sexes", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Leisure Time > Go Fly a Kite!", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 13, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe  routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to aspire", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to work towards getting something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Most people believe that both women and men should aspire to any work they want.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear when you compare people and their work.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "opportunity", "type": "name"}, {"content": "chance", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Women and men should have the equal opportunity to do any work they want to.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "task", "type": "name"}, {"content": "job", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Recent studies show that men and women think differently, and each are better at different tasks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to concentrate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to think hard about doing one thing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  So, they feel that men have got to concentrate more on these tasks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "quicker", "type": "name"}, {"content": "more rapid ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Women are quicker to notice if things disappear or are moved from one position to another. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to rotate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to move an object so it is pointing in a different direction", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Men can see an object and know more clearly how it will look if it rotates the other way. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "social", "type": "name"}, {"content": "describes a person who enjoys talking to people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Some people think that women are more social while men are more practical. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "observant", "type": "name"}, {"content": "describes a person who notices small details", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Women are observant. They notice if something is different.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob01aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "target", "type": "name"}, {"content": "object aimed at in shooting practice", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Men are better at hitting targets with darts or arrows. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob01aud09", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Expressing What is Necessary", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use certain expressions to talk about what is necessary to do in the future in order for something to happen.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " <ul><li>You have to ... </li><li>You have got to \u2026 </li><li>I'm going to have to \u2026</li><li> You need to \u2026</li>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "They feel women are going to have to work harder to do these things.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "So, they feel that men have got to concentrate more on these tasks.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Superlatives and Comparatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use adjectives to compare things. These can be either:", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Some adjectives change to different words in the comparative and superlative form. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With one syllable words, you add <span class=\"strong\">-er</span> to the adjective to make the comparative form. You add <span class=\"strong\">-est</span> to the adjective to make the superlative form. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With words of two or more syllables, you add the word <span class=\"italic\">more</span> before the adjective or adverb in the comparative form. You add <span class=\"italic\">the most</span> before the adjective or the adverb in the superlative form.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul>  \t<li>short adjectives (generally one syllable in pronunciation, e.g. fast, tall, big, large, small, etc.), or </li> \t<li>long adjectives (generally two or more syllables in pronunciation, e.g. famous, expensive, beautiful, etc.)</li> </ul>   \t\t\t", "type": "text"}, {"content": "There are different ways to use these adjectives for comparisons: two of these are comparatives and superlatives.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">Comparatives</span>: When you compare two things, you use comparatives.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">Examples:</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"> Are men better (than women) at hitting targets with darts or arrows?<br />  Are women quicker (than men) to notice if things disappear or moved from one position to another?<br />  Do women have to work harder (than man) to identify rotating items? </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">Superlatives</span>: You can also use adjectives to compare one item with the rest of a group. These are called superlative adjectives.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">Examples: </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Are men the best at hitting targets with darts or arrows? <br /> Men and women have to work together in order to do the best work.<br /> Are concentration tasks are the most difficult for men?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "As you can see, comparatives and superlatives have their specific form:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For<span class =\"strong\"> comparatives</span>, we use <span class =\"strong\">-er</span> for short adjectives and <span class =\"strong\">more + adjective</span> for long ones.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For <span class =\"strong\">superlatives</span>, we use the <span class =\"strong\">-est</span> for short adjectives and the <span class =\"strong\">most + adjective</span> for long ones.", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Draw a line dividing a large piece of paper in two.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Draw a line at the top. Write the headings Men and Women above the line, one on each side. This is a T-graph.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk to 10 people. Ask them how they see men and women. How are they different?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Complete the T-chart with words, expressions or sentences on each side.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your T-chart to the class.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I design a T-chart.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk to 10 people about the differences between men and women.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present the T-chart.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn6le13ob01re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn6le13ob01re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "Most people believe that women and men should have the same opportunity to aspire to any work they want. This does not mean that they are identical. Some people think that women are more social while men are more practical. Recent studies show that men and women think differently, and each are better at different tasks."}, {"image": "engenn6le13ob01re2img02.jpg", "time": "18500", "id": 2, "text": "Some feel that men are better at hitting targets with darts or arrows. They think that men can also find hidden objects in a picture more accurately than women. They say that men can look at an object and know more clearly how it will look if it rotates the other way. They feel women are going to have to work harder to do these things."}, {"image": "engenn6le13ob01re2img03.jpg", "time": "34000", "id": 3, "text": "Many people say that women are faster than men at recognizing if things are similar or different. Women, they feel, are observant. They are quicker to notice if things disappear or are moved from one position to another. Some say that women are good at working with small objects. So, they feel that men have got to concentrate more on these tasks."}, {"image": "engenn6le13ob01re2img01.jpg", "time": "51000", "id": 4, "text": "A conclusion is that men and women have to work together in order to do the best work."}], "audiosrc": "engenn6le13ob01re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn6le13ob01re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises